{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed168776016/6/codegen_prompts/3.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/6`\n- 题号：`3`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed168776016/6/3.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"3\">\n- `description`：识别每个封闭区域内的\"种子\"像素颜色，然后用该颜色沿区域边界内侧描边，描边宽度由种子像素的数量决定。\n- `Input structure`：背景为black。网格中有若干个由grey像素绘制的封闭多边形轮廓（轮廓线宽为1像素，轮廓形状为简单的直角多边形——所有边都是水平或垂直的）。每个封闭区域内部（black区域）包含1到3个同色的散布\"种子\"像素点，不同区域内的种子颜色各不相同。种子像素不接触grey轮廓线。\n- `Rule`：对每个grey轮廓围成的封闭区域：（1）找到区域内所有种子像素，记录其颜色C和数量N。（2）保留grey轮廓不变。（3）从grey轮廓向内，将紧贴轮廓内侧的N层像素（即内部black像素中，与轮廓的最短路径步数不超过N的那些像素）全部填充为颜色C。这里步数指上下左右四方向每步移动1像素、且不穿越grey轮廓的步数。若N=1则只填最内圈紧贴轮廓的那一层，N=2则填两层，以此类推。（4）种子像素本身所在位置也参与填充判定——如果它在填充范围内则被覆盖为C（与C同色，无变化），如果不在填充范围内则保持为C。\n- `Key insight`：种子像素承担双重角色——其颜色决定填充色，其数量决定填充厚度。解题者容易注意到颜色映射但可能忽略\"数量即厚度\"这一隐蔽的第二层编码。区域形状的多样性使得\"向内描边\"的视觉效果各不相同，增加了归纳难度。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：eval/8b7bacbf, eval/4c3d4a41, eval/332f06d7, eval/581f7754, eval/9385bd28, train/5623160b, eval/271d71e2, eval/dbff022c\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"8b7bacbf\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.4254\nmechanism=0.5043\nlexical=0.0122\ncode_feature=0.6667\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:counter, object:closed_region, object:grid_edge, object:marker, object:path, operation:count, operation:flood_fill, operation:translate, relation:adjacent, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/8b7bacbf.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/8b7bacbf.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nFill enclosed regions along a line seeded by unique border pixels.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- Colored lines/drawings on the grid.\n- Unique single-pixel colors on the grid border mark seed endpoints of each line.\n\nRule:\n- Each border seed pixel connects (8-connected) to a line drawing.\n- Find closed bg cavities whose boundary touches that line.\n- Flood-fill each such cavity with the seed pixel's color.\n\nKey insight: Only cavities reachable through the seed's own line get filled; the seed's unique color acts as a per-line fill label.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Find single pixels on grid edges that are endpoints of lines, trace along the line to find connected closed regions, and fill those regions with the edge pixel's color.\",\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"single colored pixels s on grid edge that are endpoints of a line\",\n  \"dst\": \"closed regions d connected to the line\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"d is reachable by following the line from s\",\n  \"path\": \"trace along the continuous line from edge pixel s\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"fill interior of each closed region d encountered along path with s.color\",\n  \"transform\": \"d.interior.color = s.color\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": null,\n  \"multi_step\": \"Step 1: identify single pixels on grid edge; Step 2: trace the line connected to each edge pixel; Step 3: for each closed region touching the line, flood-fill its interior with edge pixel color\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    \"flood-fill\",\n    \"path-tracing\",\n    \"edge-detection\",\n    \"region-filling\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"4c3d4a41\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3436\nmechanism=0.4256\nlexical=0.0137\ncode_feature=0.4286\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:counter, object:grid_edge, object:path, object:sprite, operation:bfs_distance, operation:translate, relation:direction, relation:inside, relation:overlap, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/4c3d4a41.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/4c3d4a41.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nFit a grey bar into a grey frame by aligning projections with colored columns, then stack colors above.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg, a grey structural color forming two components: a large rectangular frame (slot) and a smaller bar with upward projections.\n- Colored pixels inside the slot mark target columns.\n\nRule:\n- Move the bar upward into the slot so its bottom edge sits one cell above the slot's interior bottom.\n- Shift it horizontally so the bar's upward projections align column-wise with the colored pixels in the slot.\n- Stack the colored pixels immediately above the bar projections in each column.\n\nKey insight: The bar's projections act as keys that must align with the colored-column \"locks\" in the slot.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Grey horizontal bars with upward projections move upward into semi-open grey slots, aligning projections with slot openings, then colored pixels within slots move upward to align vertically with the bar's projections\",\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"grey horizontal bar with upward vertical projections s\",\n  \"dst\": \"semi-open grey slot region with downward colored vertical projections d\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s.projections align vertically with d.colored_projections (column positions match)\",\n  \"path\": \"\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"\",\n  \"transform\": \"\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": null,\n  \"multi_step\": \"Step 1: Identify grey bar s with upward projections and grey slot d with colored downward projections; Step 2: Move s upward into d such that s.projections fit into d.openings with projection-to-projection vertical alignment; Step 3: Move colored pixels upward so they align with bar projections, with bar bottom 1 cell above slot bottom\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    \"projection-slot alignment\",\n    \"vertical translation\",\n    \"geometric fitting\",\n    \"column alignment\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"The key geometric constraint: projections of the bar must align column-wise with the colored projections in the slot; movement distance varies based on projection lengths to achieve final alignment with 1-cell gap at bottom\",\n  \"type2\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src2\": \"colored pixels c within the slot region\",\n  \"dst2\": \"\",\n  \"match_cond2\": \"\",\n  \"path2\": \"move(c, direction='up') such that c.projections align vertically with s.projections and s.bottom_edge is 1 cell above slot.bottom_edge\",\n  \"trajectory2\": \"\",\n  \"transform2\": \"\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"332f06d7\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3678\nmechanism=0.4356\nlexical=0.0148\ncode_feature=0.5714\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:counter, object:marker, object:path, operation:count, operation:flood_fill, operation:translate, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/332f06d7.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/332f06d7.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nSlide a solid square through a winding channel to reach a same-sized target square.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg (most common color). A river color forms a winding corridor.\n- Two same-sized NxN solid squares on the river: mover and destination, each a distinct color.\n\nRule:\n- The mover square travels along the river toward the destination.\n- It can only pass through positions where the full NxN area is river.\n- If reachable, the mover replaces the destination; otherwise it stops at the farthest reachable point.\n- The mover's original position is filled with the river color.\n\nKey insight: Chokepoints narrower than N pixels block the square, forcing it to stop short.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"black square\",\n  \"path\": \"blue pixels \\\"water channel\\\" that is wide enough to pass through until \\\"stuck\\\" because of too narrow\",\n  \"dst\": \"reach same sized red square or \\\"get stuck\\\" on the way where the blue path is too narrow\",\n  \"transform\": \"cover the red square if reaching it\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"581f7754\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3582\nmechanism=0.4054\nlexical=0.0127\ncode_feature=0.6667\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:counter, object:grid_edge, object:marker, object:sprite, operation:translate, relation:adjacent, relation:direction, relation:inside, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/581f7754.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/581f7754.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nSlide multi-color sprites to align their marker pixels with matching isolated border anchors.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- Multi-color sprites in the interior; each has a minority-color \"marker\" pixel.\n- Isolated border pixels (non-bg with all 4-neighbors bg) act as anchors.\n\nRule:\n- Match each sprite to the border anchor sharing its marker color.\n- Top/bottom-edge anchor (non-corner): slide sprite horizontally so marker column = anchor column.\n- Left/right-edge anchor (or corner): slide sprite vertically so marker row = anchor row.\n\nKey insight: The anchor's edge position determines the slide axis — top/bottom means horizontal, left/right (or corner) means vertical.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"multi-color sprite s with a unique marker color (minority color inside s)\",\n  \"dst\": \"align to isolated border pixel d (same marker color)\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s.marker.color == d.color\",\n  \"transform\": \"translate s: if d on top/bottom edge → align col(s.marker) to col(d); else → align row(s.marker) to row(d); clip out-of-bounds pixels\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"9385bd28\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3513\nmechanism=0.4629\nlexical=0.0112\ncode_feature=0.2857\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:counter, object:marker, object:path, object:sprite, operation:bfs_distance, operation:count, operation:flood_fill, operation:translate, relation:adjacent, relation:direction, relation:overlap, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/9385bd28.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/9385bd28.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nFill rectangles between diagonal marker pairs using a color legend.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg grid with a vertical legend at the bottom-left: each row is a (marker_color, fill_color) pair.\n- Scattered L-shaped corner markers of each marker color define opposite corners of axis-aligned rectangles.\n- Some markers are solid 2×2 blocks instead of corner pairs.\n\nRule:\n- Read legend bottom-to-top; for each entry find all pixels of that marker color.\n- Determine which two bbox corners carry L-shaped anchors — the *other* diagonal defines the fill region.\n- Fill the diamond (all shortest-path cells between those two corners) with the legend's fill color.\n- Solid 2×2 marker blocks are simply recolored to the fill color.\n- Later legend entries are protected from earlier fills.\n\nKey insight: The L-shaped anchors sit on the marker diagonal; the fill goes on the opposite diagonal of the bounding box.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Use a color legend at bottom-left to find diagonal marker pairs of matching color, then fill the rectangle between them with the adjacent legend color.\",\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"diagonal pixel pair s with same color forming opposite corners of a rectangle (upper corner pixel)\",\n  \"dst\": \"diagonal pixel pair d with same color forming opposite corners of a rectangle (lower corner pixel)\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s.color == d.color && s and d are diagonally opposite\",\n  \"path\": \"\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"\",\n  \"transform\": \"fill rectangle bounded by s and d with color from legend where legend.left == s.color gives fill_color = legend.right\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": \"legend is vertical stack of color pairs at bottom-left, each pair (left-right only) has marker color on left and fill color on right\",\n  \"multi_step\": \"Step 1: identify legend as vertically stacked color pairs at bottom-left corner; Step 2: process legend entries from bottom to top; Step 3: for each legend entry (marker_color on left, fill_color on right), find all diagonal pairs of marker_color pixels; Step 4: fill rectangle between each diagonal pair with fill_color\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    \"color-legend\",\n    \"diagonal-markers\",\n    \"rectangle-fill\",\n    \"ordered-processing\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"sometimes as 2x2 squares which count as two diagonal triangles; processing order matters for overlapping regions\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"6\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"5623160b\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3395\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"agent_message","text":"实现方案已经定了：\n\n1. `main()` 里把 `0` 视为黑底，自动找最常见的非黑色作为灰色轮廓。\n2. 用 `grid != grey` 的 4 连通域找所有被灰色包围、且不接触外边界的内部区域；每个区域里统计唯一种子颜色和种子数量。\n3. 对每个内部区域做一次多源 BFS：从“与灰边界相邻的区域像素”起步记为第 1 层，向内扩张，距离 `<= N` 的像素全部染成种子色。\n4. `generate_input()` 不做固定模板，改为随机放置 1 到 3 个封闭轮廓；轮廓形状在矩形、L 形、T/十字形这几类厚实直角多边形间切换，并随机旋转翻转。\n5. 生成时先构造“填充多边形”，再把其边界画成灰色、内部留黑，并在内部非贴边位置放 1 到 3 个同色种子；放置过程带间距约束，避免轮廓粘连。\n6. 写完后按要求跑 100 次变体检查、`py_compile`，再清理 `__pycache__`。"}}
